@startuml 04-sequence-task-lifecycle
title FlowAI Platform - Task Lifecycle (sequence)

autonumber

participant "Source" as Src
participant "Operator (UI)" as U
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Event Router" as ER
participant "Secret Service" as SS
participant "Executor" as EX
participant "Agent Container" as AG
participant "LLM Provider" as LLM

note over Src, U
  Tasks are created by sources directly to the Event Router.
  No API Gateway on the create path. The API Gateway is an
  auth-aware reverse proxy for everything else (state queries,
  observation, intervention, secret registration).
  The Event Router maintains an executor pool: executors register
  on startup and signal availability. ER matches pending tasks to
  available executors and dispatches.
end note

== Executor registration (on startup) ==

EX -> ER : REST POST /executors with routing_target, capacity N, metadata
ER -> ER : Register executor in pool with capacity N
ER -> ER : Initialize slots_in_use = 0
ER --> EX : 201 with executor_id

note over EX, ER
  capacity N is **configurable per executor**.
  capacity = number of **concurrent containers**
  the executor can host. Up to N tasks run in parallel
  on the same executor (one container per task).
  ER tracks slots_in_use and matches pending tasks
  to executors only when slots_in_use is less than capacity.
end note

== Executor first ready signal ==

EX -> ER : REST POST /executors/:id/ready
ER -> ER : Mark executor as having N free slots

== Submit (source -> ER direct) ==

Src -> ER : REST POST /tasks (bearer_token, prompt, tools, secret_ids)
ER -> SS : REST open env (validate secret_ids exist)
SS --> ER : ok
ER -> ER : Build scope (HMAC: project, task, secret_ids, TTL)
ER -> ER : Persist task with status=queued, scope_token, routing_target
ER --> Src : 202 task_id

== Subscribe (UI -> GW -> ER) ==

U -> GW : WS connect (bearer_token)
GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
GW -> ER : REST subscribe to task_id events
ER -> GW : subscription ack
GW -> U : WS upgrade ack

== Dispatch (ER waits for available slot) ==

note over ER
  ER has a pending task and an executor
  whose routing_target matches AND
  whose slots_in_use is less than capacity
  (i.e., the executor has at least one free slot
  for a new parallel task).
end note

ER -> ER : Match pending task to executor X with routing_target matches, slots_in_use less than capacity
ER -> ER : UPDATE task status=dispatched, executor_id=X
ER -> ER : slots_in_use = slots_in_use plus 1
ER -> EX : REST POST /dispatch with task_spec and scope_token
EX -> SS : REST open env with scope_token
SS --> EX : env-style keys
EX -> EX : Pull image
EX -> AG : Start container, mount secrets as env / tmpfs

note over AG, EX
  Agent is a black box. Runs initial instructions. No platform API.
end note

AG -> LLM : Prompt + history
LLM --> AG : Completion or tool_use

== Agent loop (event fanout via REST) ==

loop agent loop
  AG --> EX : stdout (event stream)
  EX -> ER : REST POST /events { task_id, kind, payload }
  ER -> ER : Persist event in ER DB
  ER -> GW : REST push (event to subscribers)
  GW -> U : WS push (live)

  opt Operator intervenes
    U -> GW : inject message / cancel / rerun (WS frame, bearer_token)
    GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
    GW -> ER : REST POST /control { task_id, action }
    ER -> EX : REST POST /control { task_id, action }
    EX --> AG : forward (or stop)
  end

  AG -> LLM : Next prompt
  LLM --> AG : Next completion
end

== Finalize ==

AG --> EX : final result (stdout / exit code)
EX -> ER : REST POST /events with status=terminal, result
ER -> ER : UPDATE task status to terminal in ER DB
ER -> ER : slots_in_use = slots_in_use minus 1
ER -> GW : REST push (final event)
GW -> U : WS final
ER --> Src : callback (if configured)

== Executor returns to pool ==

EX -> ER : REST POST /executors/:id/ready signal available for next task
ER -> ER : Mark executor as having at least one free slot
note over ER
  ER is back to waiting.
  If slots_in_use is less than capacity,
  the next pending task (if any) can be
  matched to this executor immediately.
  If slots_in_use equals capacity minus one
  (i.e., this completion was the last running task),
  the EX is now fully idle and ready to take
  capacity new tasks.
end note

note over AG, EX
  Container terminated. Scope token expires.
end note

@enduml